{
  "case_id": "2010-09-996",
  "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We'll hear argument next this morning in Case 09-996, Walker v. Martin."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Todd Marshall",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Charles Martin never adequately explained why he waited more than 5 years to present additional claims to the California Supreme Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what about the charge that, yes, we can agree with you that in general 5 years seems like a long time, but we have a brief from the Habeas Corpus Resource Center that says that in the 5- to 6-year delay category, 62 percent are dismissed on the merits, and that you can't tell; sometimes they do it on the merits, sometimes they do it as time-barred,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Todd Marshall",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first is that to measure summary denials, you can't tell from a summary denial ruling what the court was thinking about the time of delay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So basically you're taking the position or you're conceding that the California courts are not consistent in their application of the timeliness rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there some Federal rule that says you have to apply a procedural ground before you decide the merits?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Todd Marshall",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Robbins case specifically provided that a 5-month window from the discovery of triggering facts to the presentation of the -- of the claim was a reasonable amount of time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When does the State think that Mr. Martin's claim became untimely?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But -- but the cases that you're using in which we insisted upon adequacy in the sense of equal treatment of equal people are cases in which the effect of the State decision was to exclude the matter from Federal -- from Federal supervision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MARSHALL: This Court has also required legitimate State interests, and this Court has used the legitimate State interests context, like, for example, in Smith v. Texas, where this Court has declared a particular kind of violation was a constitutional violation and the Court exercised its discretion not to reach the violation, this Court found that the State had no legitimate State interest in such a ruling."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But none of this is -- is a device as is used in the cases that -- that you are referring to that go into adequacy, a device to exclude the Federal courts from the case. That's -- that's not what's going on here, is it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0001-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MICHAEL B. BIGELOW ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, Mr. Bigelow, is that right? I take your point that nobody can say exactly when Mr. Martin's claims became untimely, but 5 years is untimely, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Why was this petition not filed for 5 years?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you really need case law to tell you that 5 years is not as promptly as circumstances permit when you -- when you have no justification?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Bigelow, isn't this similar to the rule that governed Federal habeas review prior to AEDPA?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bigelow",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Approximately 2,500, give or take."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bigelow",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's the problem. That's the problem. The test that is applied without guidelines, without any kind of guidelines. Judicial discretion -- judicial discretion is informed discretion; it is not discretion -- it's -- it's judgment pursuant to known guidelines. It is not a judgment issued pursuant to inclination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You may be -- you'd better be careful about what you wish for because I am not sure that the kind of system that's being proposed is going to be better for habeas applicants than the one that California now has. We really don't know that, do we?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ba92229bce6d2403139f776d028d70ff3fc161f4612fb82d8a7d2db7bd634c18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ba92229bce6d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-996",
      "confidence": 0.0,
